:: Event - Gone in the night [Place]
<h1 class="ptitle"><<=$game.cabinName ?? ''>></h1>
<br />
<<set _gnB = $game.betrayal>>
<<if !_gnB>>
	<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
<</if>>
<<set _gnNpc = _gnB.npc>>
<<set _gnShe = setup.pronounceWhat(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnHer = setup.pronounceWho(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnHers = setup.pronounceWhos(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnGender = 'gender-' + setup.genderClass(_gnNpc)>>

<center>
	<<image 'places/cabin/gone_in_the_night.jpg'>>
</center>
<br />

<<set _gnWitnesses = $guests.filter(function (g) { return setup.getAge(g) >= 18 && g.id !== _gnNpc.id; })>>
<<set _gnWitness = _gnWitnesses.length ? setup.getRandomElement(_gnWitnesses) : null>>

<<if _gnB.kind === 'theft'>>
	The back door was hanging open when you came down. The storeroom had been picked over in the dark, quickly and quietly, by someone who knew exactly where everything was. <strong><<=setup.betrayal.lootText(_gnB.loot)>></strong> were gone. <span @class="''+_gnGender+''" style="font-weight:bold"><<=_gnNpc.name>></span>'s bed hadn't been slept in.
	<br /><br />
	<<if _gnWitness>>
		<<sayNpc _gnWitness>>
			<<=_gnNpc.name>> was talking about leaving all week. I thought it was just talk. I should've said something.
		<</sayNpc>>
		<br />
	<</if>>
	One set of prints led from the back door to the treeline, deep at the heel the way they are when someone carries more than <<=_gnShe>> came with. It was still early. <<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> couldn't be far.
<<elseif _gnB.kind === 'intel'>>
	Nothing was missing, which was exactly what bothered you. The gate had been left unlatched before dawn, and <span @class="''+_gnGender+''" style="font-weight:bold"><<=_gnNpc.name>></span>'s bed was empty.
	<br /><br />
	<<if _gnWitness>>
		<<sayNpc _gnWitness>>
			I saw <<=_gnHer>> out by the road before it got light. <<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> was heading toward <<=_gnB.leak.name>>'s land. I thought <<=_gnShe>> was just going for a walk.
		<</sayNpc>>
		<br />
	<</if>>
	<<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> had spent weeks inside your walls. <<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> knew where the guards stood, how thin the night watch was, how many people slept in the house. And <<=_gnShe>> was taking all of it to <strong><<=_gnB.leak.name>></strong>.
<<else>>
	A folded piece of paper sat on the kitchen table, weighed down with a cup, your name on it in careful, uneven handwriting.
	<br /><br />
	<<if _gnNpc.relationship < 0>>
		<em>I never wanted to be here. I did what I was told and I kept my mouth shut. Don't come looking for me.</em>
	<<else>>
		<em>I tried. I really did. But I can't keep living like this, and I'd rather go before I turn into someone I don't like. Thank you for the food. Please don't come after me.</em>
	<</if>>
	<br /><br />
	<span @class="''+_gnGender+''" style="font-weight:bold"><<=_gnNpc.name>></span> was gone before sunrise. The bed was made.
<</if>>
<br /><br />

<div id="gn_chase">
	<<if _gnB.kind === 'note'>>
		<<set _gnChaseLabel = 'Go after ' + _gnHer + ' and talk'>>
		<<linkreplace _gnChaseLabel>>
			<<run $('#gn_leave').hide()>>
			<<addmins 90>>
			<<set _gnChance = _gnNpc.relationship >= 0 ? 65 : 35>>
			<<if setup.percentageChance(_gnChance)>>
				You caught up with <<=_gnHer>> where the road bent away from the river, sitting on a rock with <<=_gnHers>> bag between <<=_gnHers>> feet, not even pretending to be surprised.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _gnNpc>>
					I knew you'd come. Fine. One more chance. But things have to change.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				<<set _gnNpc.happy = Math.max(_gnNpc.happy ?? 0, -30)>>
				<<set _gnNpc.relationship = Math.max(_gnNpc.relationship ?? 0, 5)>>
				<<run $guests.push(_gnNpc)>>
				<<run setup.npc.addHistory(_gnNpc, 'returned')>>
				<<unset $game.betrayal>>
				<strong>(<<=_gnNpc.name>> came back. Happy −30 and Relationship at least 5. She will leave again if nothing changes.)</strong>
			<<else>>
				You found <<=_gnHers>> tracks, and then you lost them at the river. When you finally saw <<=_gnHer>> it was across the water, a small figure not looking back.
				<br /><br />
				<<unset $game.betrayal>>
				<<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> was gone.
			<</if>>
			<br /><br />
			<<link 'Head back'>>
				<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
			<</link>>
		<</linkreplace>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _gnChaseLabel = 'Go after ' + _gnHer>>
		<<link _gnChaseLabel>>
			<<addmins 90>>
			<<set $enemies = [clone(_gnB.npc)]>>
			<<fight $enemies 'Event - Gone in the night - won' 'Event - Gone in the night - lost'>>
		<</link>>
	<</if>>
</div>
<div id="gn_leave">
	<<set _gnLeaveLabel = 'Let ' + _gnHer + ' go'>>
	<<linkreplace _gnLeaveLabel>>
		<<run $('#gn_chase').hide()>>
		<<if _gnB.kind === 'theft'>>
			You stood in the empty storeroom a while. Then you shut the door and told the others there was nothing to be done. Some of them nodded. Some of them looked at the locks.
		<<elseif _gnB.kind === 'intel'>>
			You told the guards to double the watch and left it at that. You'd never know how much <<=_gnNpc.name>> had already told, only that <strong><<=_gnB.leak.name>></strong> would be ready for you now.
		<<else>>
			You read the note twice, folded it and put it in your pocket. Some people just can't stay.
		<</if>>
		<<unset $game.betrayal>>
		<br /><br />
		<<link 'Continue'>>
			<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
		<</link>>
	<</linkreplace>>
</div>


:: Event - Gone in the night - won [Place]
<h1 class="ptitle"><<=$game.cabinName ?? ''>></h1>
<br />
<<set _gnB = $game.betrayal>>
<<if !_gnB>>
	<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
<</if>>
<<set _gnNpc = _gnB.npc>>
<<set _gnShe = setup.pronounceWhat(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnHer = setup.pronounceWho(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnHers = setup.pronounceWhos(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnCaptured = $slaves.some(function (s) { return s.id === _gnB.npc.id; })>>
<<set _gnKilled = $prevFight?.defeatedEnemies?.[0]?.killed ?? false>>
<<run setup.betrayal.returnLoot(_gnB.loot)>>
<<run setup.settlements.undoLeakIntel(_gnB.leak)>>

<<if _gnB.kind === 'theft'>>
	Everything was still in <<=_gnHers>> pack. You went through it on the ground, item by item, and took back <strong><<=setup.betrayal.lootText(_gnB.loot)>></strong>.
<<else>>
	<<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> hadn't reached <<=_gnB.leak.name>> yet. Whatever <<=_gnShe>> knew about your base, it went no further than <<=_gnHers>> own head.
<</if>>
<br /><br />
<<if _gnCaptured>>
	You walked <<=_gnHer>> home with <<=_gnHers>> hands tied. Nobody in the yard said a word as you took <<=_gnHer>> down to the basement.
<<elseif _gnKilled>>
	<<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> didn't get up. You covered <<=_gnHer>> and went home.
<<else>>
	You left <<=_gnHer>> in the dirt, bleeding and cursing, and started back before <<=_gnShe>> could think of anything else to try.
<</if>>
<<unset $game.betrayal>>
<br /><br />
<<link 'Head back'>>
	<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
<</link>>


:: Event - Gone in the night - lost [Place]
<h1 class="ptitle"><<=$game.cabinName ?? ''>></h1>
<br />
<<set _gnB = $game.betrayal>>
<<if !_gnB>>
	<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
<</if>>
<<set _gnNpc = _gnB.npc>>
<<set _gnShe = setup.pronounceWhat(_gnNpc)>>
<<set _gnHers = setup.pronounceWhos(_gnNpc)>>

<<=ucfirst(_gnShe)>> was faster than you thought, and meaner. By the time you could stand again, the treeline was empty and <<=_gnHers>> tracks had gone into the water.
<br /><br />
<<if _gnB.kind === 'theft'>>
	<<=setup.betrayal.lootText(_gnB.loot)>> were gone for good.
<<else>>
	<<=_gnB.leak.name>> would know your base by tomorrow.
<</if>>
<<unset $game.betrayal>>
<br /><br />
<<link 'Limp home'>>
	<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
<</link>>
